  "name": "ball-and-plate-swing",
  "$comment": "Open loop: the plate swings about y as alpha = -2.0 deg cos(2 pi 2.0 Hz t), prescribed through a stiff lock spring driven by an MSf; the ball starts at rest 0.10 m from the axis. The 3D rolling contact includes the plate's rotation rate (centrifugal drift outwards) and acceleration (the ball centre is 15.7 mm above the axis); the signal chain LinX integrates the linearised x'' = 5/7 g sin(alpha) of the same plate angle. Both are checked against design.py.",
